Z||000023||DaRkLoRD||10-18-2001||07:40 PM||||Anyone who knows me will probably say I'm pretty conservative (modest, quiet, and serious..) most of the time.. but..?<P>one of my lifetime goals is to someday build childrens hospitals in poor countries, as well as shelters for street kids.. I realize that this wouldn't get me any money. I also don't like pollution.. or freeloaders. the canadian welfare system is abused to such an extent that it's a damn joke.. same with our health care system. It's nice being able to go to the hospital and receive whatever treatment you require, and not worrying about how you'll pay for it.. I've had 2 cat scans in the last 4 months, numerous x-rays, and soon an MRI.. in the USA that would cost me several thousand dollars.. but instead, it comes off my taxes.. I digress... I would love to see the welfare system totally overhauled.. and photo ID for all immigrants, and maybe all citizens... I don't like invasions of my privacy.. but I have to wear a security badge at work as it's a secure location.. I don't mind.. I already carry government ID, several cards actually.. what's the big deal about having one specifically for ID?<P>I don't think we should put profit before the environment, or other people.. (ie. sweatshops) I see nothing wrong with giving food and supplies to refugees who are against our enemies.. then again, I also think that the USA should stay out of the business of other countries..<P>I'm not much of a pacifist.. if someone mugs me, unless they're armed with a firearm, I WILL fight back.. same goes for someone who breaks into my home. If someone breaks into my house and I perceive a threat to myself or my loved ones, I will defend myself/them. I'd have no problem whatsoever knocking a person out and tying them up until the police arrived.. same with locking them in a room.. oh wait, that's "entrapment" (or was it "man trapping"? I forget..) and I'd get in trouble for that... I'd fight that charge, they had no business being there in the first place..<P>I can't decide if I'm more liberal or conservative.. in canada, those political parties aren't quite the same as in the usa.. we have the "conservatives", but they're almost the same as our "liberals".. we have more extreme ones, such as the NDP (socialist) and the alliance (really conservative... formerly called the reform party. rayb would love these guys...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> heh)<P>anyway, I think that's enough rambling for now. I forgot what my original point was, so I'll shut up.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||4
