Z||000027||EdsB52||10-19-2001||04:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B><BR>And I wouldn't want Clinton to be president now.  Like he would command any respect, here or abroad.  Or like Madeline Albright would, either.  In fact, weren't she and Donna Shalala and Ruth Bader Ginsberg three of the original munchkins in the Wizard of Oz??  Clinton has always like hollywood types around him!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"rayb,  I'm not sure why you are equating Clinton being back with the market being up, as if somehow those two events were related.  The market was slowing down BEFORE Clinton left office, and was surging BEFORE he took office."<P>So are you saying the market was recovering as a result of Bush Sr's actions, and slowing as a result of Clinton's actions? Or are you being realistic and saying that the President has little to do with the economy? Anyone with sense realizes that Greenspan has much to do with the upturns/downturns of the general economy through interest rates, hence indirectly the stock market. <P>As far as the stock market goes, it closed higher at the end of the Bush Sr era than it did when he took office. The same is true of the Clinton era, except it made a larger % rate of gains. ||||reg||1
