Z||000029||Oreif||10-19-2001||08:36 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>WHY IS BUSH AFRAID OF NATION BUILDING?????<BR>if his dad had not been and wiped out sadamm in gulf war and put in a liberal gov in irock<BR>or helped afgan before taliban took over we would not have this mess now.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First, Bush Sr. was forced to stop the war with Iraq (It's a country not a car.) because the U.N. would not allow the government (Saddam) to be removed from power or replaced. The U.N. only wanted them out of Kuwait. In fact the U.N. wanted us to stop as soon as they left Kuwait but the many countries in the coalition were able to convince the majority that we needed to remove the threat of attack from Kuwait also.<P>The Taliban taking power back in the mid 90's was actually a step in the positive direction for Afghanistan. After Russia left the country was controlled by territorial warlords. The Taliban stepped in and organized things. The problem with them was once in power, they let the power get to their heads, and their ideals get swayed by Osama Bin Laden. Many extremists over the years have been able to come to power by distorting their ideals onto others.<BR>We did not know back then that the Taliban would be swayed by OBL distorted views. <BR>Much in the same way you have anti-religeous views.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||Formula88||10-19-2001||09:04 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>Wait a minute; you're busting Ray's balls for being grammatically incorrect while being factually viable, and you miswrote? By your context, I believe you meant to write, 'unintelligible.' Besides, have you ever spoken with Ray?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm not busting his balls just for grammar.  His posts are largely unintelligible due to his haphazard way of writing.  You are correct in that I meant to write unintelligible and wrote intelligible by mistake.  I'm not claiming to be perfect, nor am I claiming that my views are right and his are wrong.  I was simply stating that people will take him more seriously if he takes the time to word his posts so people can understand him.  I disagree with a lot you have to say, but your posts are more clearly worded.  At least I have a better idea of what you mean, instead of having to guess and try to pull some meaning out of a chaotic post.<P>As far as his views being factually viable, that's debatable.  His views are so extreme as to hinder their believability.  There are few absolutes in life, and especially in politics.  It's all shades of gray and not simply black and white.  There are several factual mistakes in his posts.  One of which Orief pointed out by mentioning that Bush Sr. couldn't go after Saddam himself once Iraq was out of Kuwait because the UN wouldn't let us.  It was a coalition of forces, not the US vs. Iraq.  We had to abide by what the coalition wanted to acheive, not just what US interests were.  I think it was a mistake leaving Saddam in power, but it would have ignited an international powder keg to go after him when the rest of the coalition is saying stop.<P>And on your last point, I fail to see how it could matter whether or not I've met Ray in person.  No, I haven't.  All the more reason to word his posts more clearly.  If the post is the only communication people have with you, then that's the only way you have to influence them or build a reputation.||||reg||3
