Z||000044||EdsB52||10-19-2001||02:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Hi EdsB52,<P>You are right with me.  I wasn't blaming Clinton or giving him credit.  He was largely irrelevant regarding the economy, or most of what went on in the country during his terms for that matter, other than giving the presidency a black eye.  But Greenspan had more to do with how the economy went, as well as just the technology in the private sector.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Good, glad to see you don't buy into the fallacy that the President has the most to do with the economy. However, we have a paradox here. Who appoints Greenspan? Who confirms Greenspan? Reagan, the Clinton, who, through my memory extended him for 12 or 15 more years. So Clinton can indirectly be given credit for the economy, unless a person thinks Greenspan sucks, then given the blame.<P>Now, as for giving the Presidency a black eye, who cares? I'm politically moderate-left, but feel Nixon was the best President we've enjoyed in recent times and he gave the Presidency a black eye as well. To me, it's far more egregious to fix an election than to screw an intern and lie about it. Or, as in the case of Reagan/Bush, perform the deeds of the Iran-Contra and get dork to lie for you. Why do people bash Clinton (for whom I didn't vote), because he got over and is having fun. America enjoyed the greatest prosperity ever during these years (not crediting Clinton), so why is everyone bitter?<P>Don't forget Andrew Johnson, successor to Abraham Lincoln was the first President to be impeached, and Roosevelt (Democrat) was credited for WWII success and departure from the Hoover initiated depression. So for all the party specific folks, the Republicans have left more black eyes on the Presidency than Democrats, in case your keeping score.<P>"One parting shot at Clinton (it's so easy).  Remember when we kept hearing "character doesn't matter"?  Turns out it did, and it does."<P>I don't remember hearing that, but I agree with it. OK, how does it? Character, which a President like Reagan was assigned plenty of, makes us feel fuzzy inside, but doesn't get things done. Who cares if the President is whore or a queer? Again, this is another ad hominem sellout to care about the personal reputation of a person, as opposed to the professional reputation. Example: I went to the dentist yesterday to get 2 implants (screws into the jaw) installed in my mouth. The dentist is a bald old man with a quick temper. I checked the licensing board before I had him work on me and he had 1 complaint in 30 years of work that was dismissed. I care more about professional reputation than lip service and people that make me feel fuzzy. My general practitioner has had 14 complaints in 10 years, but they're all billing complaints and not quality complaints so I proceed on with her. She seems very competent, but has tried to screw me with billing, so I got everything straight before we pressed on.||||reg||1
Z||000045||EdsB52||10-19-2001||02:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Man, I just can't stay away from this crap.<P>Formula - the world is full of morons.  Looks like we found some on PFF.  I don't think they're worth replying to.<P>RaYB=EVIL=eds52 BS=LIBERALISTS=BADDER GRAMMER=WIERd IdEAS=HED-UP-TEH-A$$=NEVR ENGDING CARP<P>---------------<BR>Question Wierd and Wonder WHy youre Stupid<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, it's bible thumping freak, little bitchtek. I hope you didn't spend too much time thinking of all this stuff, it's sooooo divine. By the way, Jesus's little fag, what is a "NEVR ENGDING CARP?" Is it some kind of fisherman's dream? You're the sh!t I scrape off the bottom of my shoe before entering the house.||||reg||1
