Z||000059||BN Boomer||10-19-2001||07:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by EdsB52:<BR><B>America enjoyed the greatest prosperity ever during these years (not crediting Clinton), so why is everyone bitter?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oh gee, how about because:<P>Clinton and his enviro-freaks took all sorts of back door action (Executive Orders, probably used more than any other president in history) to do what they couldn't through legitimate democratic process. Creating baloney national monuments. Huge roadless areas. Even existing roads are being gated off or outright destroyed. Would you like some pictures? The Dems claim we don't have the funds to maintain existing forest service roads, yet somehow they can find the money to run bulldozers with rippers down miles of roads, plant vegetation, undercut banks so they will collapse, rip out drainage systems, etc. <P>How about Hillary style socialized health care, anyone? (Geez, if WE implemented it, too, where would the Canadians then go to get timely health care?) Yeah just what we need, another bloated beauracracy limiting our freedom and options, but this time with the power to deem what health care THEY think is necessary and deny what they do not. <P>Gun control that is purely symbolic in action but creates a market where I have to pay an additional $500 if I want something as deadly as a freaking BAYONET LUG (How many drive by stabbings have you heard of lately???), collapsible/folding stock (Due to the excessive number of drive by buttstroking, too, I imagine), or a flash suppressor on a semi-automatic rifle that also happens to have an equally deadly pistol grip. What a f*cking joke. Even Canadians with their considerably more stringent gun control laws are still allowed to to have such "dangerous" items on new firearms.<P>You know what the funny thing is? While I was disappointed that Clinton got elected in the first place, I decided to give him a chance before making any final opinions.<P>How do you feel about the fact that your fellow "progressives" would like nothing more than to see your Fiero crushed and recycled and for you to be forced to ride public transportation for the remainder of your life? Or how about $5 a gallon for gasoline?<BR>||||reg||1
