Z||000067||BN Boomer||10-20-2001||02:41 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B><P>yes BUT ONLY IF YOU ARE A JEW and ONLY WITH 5-10 BILLION IN OUT SIDE HELP arabs arenot wellcome to share it in their own birthlands.<P>mormans ran utah their way and other that a few wars with the USA mostly still do.<BR>womans rights or civil rights are both very new ideas to them.[hay bro does that mean that i must treat #1 wife the same as #3wife.]OLD WAYS I KNOW.<BR>as is the idea that non-morman's have any rights at all.<BR>BUT THEN I NEVER LIKED MIND CONTROL ANYWAY!!<BR>MY PEOPLE BUILD THIS LAND BUT WERE VERY EARY ATHIEST AND WERE TOO BUSY RUNING FROM REGILION'S NUT'S TO CHASE ANY OF THEM<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, next you are going to tell us how we don't give any foreign aid to Arab countries. Or pump illions into their economies through the purchase of oil. And I think the Israeli's DO want to co-exist peacefully with their Arab neighbors. It's the radical Arabs who want to exterminate the Jews. In any order to maintain any semblance of order in their, Israel simply has to respond to Palestinian violence with the level of force that they do.<P>As far as the Mormons, you conveniently forgot to name any specific instances of the events you named. When were they at war with the USA? Why do you think they moved to Utah? Because intolerant people like you wouldn't leave them alone anywhere else, that's why. <BR>You are obviously so totally ignorant on these subjects that it is impossible to attempt to have any sort of rational debate with you. The amount of research, thought, and knowledge that you put into your posts appears to be about par with the effort you put into communicating in a coherent manner. Little to none.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000068||maryjane||10-20-2001||07:53 AM||||Funny thing about all those in your list. None allowed freedom of religion. It is "believe as we say, or your punished or killed" Well, for the most part anyway. I don't know that much about Mormons or Utah. With the exception of Iran and Afganistan, I don't know of any other nation that has a govt that is run by religion, on the right or left. They are run by people and politicians or dictators. The first thing Cromwell did was to call for the dismemberment of the church,"by root and branch". If you were English, he was a great man, if Scottish, the devil himself. Hitler was neither religious or atheist. He viewed himself as a god on earth, but not in the religious sense. Only in a racist sense. I'll address your challenge at the end of this post, but first: I've read some of your posts regarding the many wars that were caused by religion of one sort of another. None, in fact were. Religion may be the reason given publicly to justify them, but power, expansionism, and greed are the cause of every war I can think of.<BR>Crusades:-supposedly to wrest the Holy Land from the 'un-Godly Moslems and to bring back the artifacts of early christian civilizations. Britian wanted the trade revenues and taxation that it could impose on that part of the world. It was just beginning to think about it's role in the world and wanted to beat it's rival Spain and France in carving up the world for it's own needs.<BR>Papal states: This is one of those areas where it is difficult to tell whether the dog is wagging the tail or vice-versa. Clearly religion played a part on the surface, and there is no denying that thousands were imprisoned and exiled. But after reading all I could find since your challenge was posted, I believe it was again greed that drove the head of the church during this period. The church seemed to be interested 'what'(taxes, resources) it get more than 'who' it could control. It pretty much ignored the desolate provincials, but concentrated it's reign over areas with something of value to offer/be obtained. A grey area; I'll concede it to you for now. <P>Hitler: At the end of WWI, Germany was cut up into a small and un-important country by the treaty that ended the stalemate. It's navy was destroyed, restrictions were imposed on it's industry and military development. The nation was in dis-array and inflation was rampant. Hitler rose to power through the common people, not the aristocracy. He promised and wanted a return to the pre-WWI status of being a world power, with worldwide respect. He had to unite his people to a common cause, so he chose race, the pure aryan(sp) race. He blamed Germany's problems on races that were outside that of his own, in order to blind them of what he really wanted. Power and regional, then world domination. Religion had nothing to do with what he envisioned. He never wanted a master religion, just  'master-race'. But, this too was just a ruse. Hitler wanted military gains, prestige and land and went to any length to get it. The first countries he 'liberated were the low countries where people of German descent lived and were once part of the German Empire. He invaded Russia solely for the oil and natural resources. He needed France for it's agriculture. He never really wanted a war with Britain, but could not escape it after Winston C. threw in with the French.Undeniably, greed, power,lunacy, and ego. Not religion caused. Religion was a scapegoat, a red herring. <BR>Japan: Japan too had designs on being the big power in the western Pacific. Needed raw materials to fight a war of expansionism.. The U.S. placed an embargo on rubber and oil, so Japan hit Pearl to take us out of the equation. It then went ahead with it's invasion of Burma, Indonesia and China to obtain oil & rubber for it's war machine and manufactoring. Religion had nothing whatsoever to do with any of WWII. Had religion never existed, Germany and Japan would have followed the same power hungry path that history shows. Religion was a victim of the agressor nations, not the cause of the conflicts.<BR>Viet Nam/Korea: Both confilcts were caused by ideology differences. N. Korea and N Viet Nam wanted to unite their respective countries as communist enclaves. The U.S. was afraid of expanding communist influence in the region and backed the southern govts in both cases. No religion involved, either overtly or otherwise. Land, power, and greed, pure & simple.<BR>The Gulf War: Saddam H. made the same choice as Germany and Japan. Had a little oil money to spend, built a sizable military, and started looking for somewhere to expand to. Needed a port, so chose the weakest neighbor:Kuwait. He knew he couldn't take on Saudia Arabia, had fought Iran for years without success, so his choice was clear. With the oil rich kindom of Kuwait under his belt, he would be the pre-eminent power in the region, could control world wide flow of oil thru the Straits, and be in a position to control oil prices and would be looked up to by all of the mideastern countries. Saddam may have used religion as a tool to get what he wanted, but it was power and greed that drove him. Still is. We got into it to keep oil supplies steady and reliable, and to have some face-saving after our Viet Nam non-war. Again, if there were no religion at all, Saddam would still have invaded Kuwait and we would have still responded as we did.<BR>Rhodesia/Ruhwanda: these civil wars are race based and always have been. From families, tribes, and provinces. It is just one segment of the population against another. Depends who is in control at the time whether a segment of the population falls out of favor or not. <BR>Now, 'a religion run gov't that doesn't cause pain for the common people in the long term with it's right wing policies". Other than the Taliban, Iran, and the Vatican, I know of no country that is religion run. (I don't include Iraq. They are a military dictatorship.) Ours definitly is not. What are the common people? I'm a white male. I live in a state where the caucasian population is a majority only by a few percentage points. I earn just over the national poverty index. I have always held a blue collar job. I live comfortably; not extravagant, but not destitute either. I've been frugal, as has my family and have enough "on paper" assets to retire comfortably if I want now. I'm as common as they come here in Texas. THIS gov't has been very good for this common person, as it did for my farming/refinery-working father, and dustbowl farming grandfather. Lasted 225 years. France, Canada, Australia, Italy, S. Korea, Taiwan, New Zealand,Britain, Iceland, Switzerland, Finland, Greece, Japan, Thailand, Israel. All seem to be doing nicely. There will never be a utopia where all things are rosy for all people. If religion were to magically dis-appear overnight, wars would still be waged for greed and power, bigotry and racism. I do not support blue laws, (ours was repealled years ago), I'm sorry you can't buy a drink Sunday morning. You're welcome to believe anything you want to. Put the blame of everything on religion? It doesn't hold up and you know it. Put it on greed, you will be closer. Put it on predjudices and bigotry, you're a lot closer.<BR>Believe in the boogeyman if you want to, but not on the rest of us. We have our own boogeyman, and it isn't you.<BR>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>the challenge is name a religion that ran a goverment fairly well without causeing pain to the common people long term with rightwing world views.<BR>a short list of ones that failed<BR>taliban<BR>iran<BR>hitler<BR>cromwell in england<BR>spain franco<BR>most south/central american countrys<BR>pilgrims in mass<BR>mormans in utah<BR>popal states in italy<BR>holyland in crusades<BR>got any that worked, ever??????<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000069||ray b||10-20-2001||11:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Funny thing about all those in your list. None allowed freedom of religion. It is "believe as we say, or your punished or killed" Well, for the most part anyway.<P>REPLY <BR>YES AND THAT IS THE POINT OF VIEW I FEAR ABOUT BUSH AND RUSH AND THE RIGHTWING CHRISTIANS RIGHT NOW HEAR IN THE HOMELAND.<P> I don't know that much about Mormons or Utah. With the exception of Iran and Afganistan, I don't know of any other nation that has a govt that is run by religion, on the right or left. They are run by people and politicians or dictators. The first thing Cromwell did was to call for the dismemberment of the church,"by root and branch". If you were English, he was a great man, if Scottish, the devil himself.<P>ONLY IF YOU WERE ON HIS SIDE MANY ENGLISH DIED IN WARS AGAINTS HIM.<BR> Hitler was neither religious or atheist. He viewed himself as a god on earth, but not in the religious sense. Only in a racist sense.<BR>RASED CATHLOIC AND ALL IN PARTY WERE CHRISTIAN NO JEWS, GYPSY, OR ATHIEST ALLOWED.<P><BR> I'll address your challenge at the end of this post, but first: I've read some of your posts regarding the many wars that were caused by religion of one sort of another. None, in fact were. Religion may be the reason given publicly to justify them, but power, expansionism, and greed are the cause of every war I can think of.<BR>Crusades:-supposedly to wrest the Holy Land from the 'un-Godly Moslems and to bring back the artifacts of early christian civilizations. Britian wanted the trade revenues and taxation that it could impose on that part of the world. It was just beginning to think about it's role in the world and wanted to beat it's rival Spain and France in carving up the world for it's own needs.<P>RIVERS OF BLOOD IN THE STREETS AS HOLY WARRORS KILLED ALL IN THE HOLY CITY<BR>Papal states: This is one of those areas where it is difficult to tell whether the dog is wagging the tail or vice-versa. Clearly religion played a part on the surface, and there is no denying that thousands were imprisoned and exiled. But after reading all I could find since your challenge was posted, I believe it was again greed that drove the head of the church during this period. The church seemed to be interested 'what'(taxes, resources) it get more than 'who' it could control. It pretty much ignored the desolate provincials, but concentrated it's reign over areas with something of value to offer/be obtained. A grey area; I'll concede it to you for now. <P>POPE CLAIMS TO RULE IN THE NAME OF CHRIST!!<P><BR>Hitler: At the end of WWI, Germany was cut up into a small and un-important country by the treaty that ended the stalemate. It's navy was destroyed, restrictions were imposed on it's industry and military development. The nation was in dis-array and inflation was rampant. Hitler rose to power through the common people, not the aristocracy. He promised and wanted a return to the pre-WWI status of being a world power, with worldwide respect. He had to unite his people to a common cause, so he chose race, the pure aryan(sp) race. He blamed Germany's problems on races that were outside that of his own, in order to blind them of what he really wanted. Power and regional, then world domination. Religion had nothing to do with what he envisioned. He never wanted a master religion, just  'master-race'. But, this too was just a ruse. Hitler wanted military gains, prestige and land and went to any length to get it. The first countries he 'liberated were the low countries where people of German descent lived and were once part of the German Empire. He invaded Russia solely for the oil and natural resources. He needed France for it's agriculture. He never really wanted a war with Britain, but could not escape it after Winston C. threw in with the French.Undeniably, greed, power,lunacy, and ego. Not religion caused. Religion was a scapegoat, a red herring. <P>ALL THE DEAD JEWS AND GYPSY DON'T SEE IT THAT WAY<BR>Japan: Japan too had designs on being the big power in the western Pacific. Needed raw materials to fight a war of expansionism.. The U.S. placed an embargo on rubber and oil, so Japan hit Pearl to take us out of the equation. It then went ahead with it's invasion of Burma, Indonesia and China to obtain oil & rubber for it's war machine and manufactoring. Religion had nothing whatsoever to do with any of WWII. Had religion never existed, Germany and Japan would have followed the same power hungry path that history shows. Religion was a victim of the agressor nations, not the cause of the conflicts.<BR>Viet Nam/Korea: Both confilcts were caused by ideology differences. N. Korea and N Viet Nam wanted to unite their respective countries as communist enclaves. The U.S. was afraid of expanding communist influence in the region and backed the southern govts in both cases. No religion involved, either overtly or otherwise. Land, power, and greed, pure & simple.<P>KILL A COMMIE FOR CHRIST BILLBOARDS ALL OVER THE SOUTH RIGHT NEXT TO SUPPORT THE KKK ONES<BR>BUDDIEST WHO BURNED IN PROTEST OF VIET REPRESSION MAY NOT AGREE  <P><BR>The Gulf War: Saddam H. made the same choice as Germany and Japan. Had a little oil money to spend, built a sizable military, and started looking for somewhere to expand to. Needed a port, so chose the weakest neighbor:Kuwait. He knew he couldn't take on Saudia Arabia, had fought Iran for years without success, so his choice was clear. With the oil rich kindom of Kuwait under his belt, he would be the pre-eminent power in the region, could control world wide flow of oil thru the Straits, and be in a position to control oil prices and would be looked up to by all of the mideastern countries. Saddam may have used religion as a tool to get what he wanted, but it was power and greed that drove him. Still is. We got into it to keep oil supplies steady and reliable, and to have some face-saving after our Viet Nam non-war. Again, if there were no religion at all, Saddam would still have invaded Kuwait and we would have still responded as we did.<BR>Rhodesia/Ruhwanda: these civil wars are race based and always have been. From families, tribes, and provinces. It is just one segment of the population against another. Depends who is in control at the time whether a segment of the population falls out of favor or not.<P>RWANDA IS RELIGION WAR CATHLIC AGAINST PROTESTANT AND IT SPREAD 3.5 MILLION DEAD<BR>RHODESIA IS RACE BASED COMMIES.<P>Now, 'a religion run gov't that doesn't cause pain for the common people in the long term with it's right wing policies". Other than the Taliban, Iran, and the Vatican, I know of no country that is religion run. (I don't include Iraq. They are a military dictatorship.) Ours definitly is not. What are the common people? I'm a white male. I live in a state where the caucasian population is a majority only by a few percentage points. I earn just over the national poverty index. I have always held a blue collar job. I live comfortably; not extravagant, but not destitute either. I'm as common as they come here in Texas. THIS gov't has been very good for this common person, as it did for my farming/refinery-working father, and dustbowl farming grandfather. Lasted 225 years. France, Canada, Australia, Italy, S. Korea, Taiwan, New Zealand,Britain, Iceland, Switzerland, Finland, Greece, Japan, Thailand, Israel. All seem to be doing nicely. There will never be a utopia where all things are rosy for all people. If religion were to magically dis-appear overnight, wars would still be waged for greed and power, bigotry and racism. I do not support blue laws, (ours was repealled years ago), I'm sorry you can't buy a drink Sunday morning. You're welcome to believe anything you want to. Put the blame of everything on religion? It doesn't hold up and you know it. Put it on greed, you will be closer. Put it on predjudices and bigotry, you're a lot closer.<BR>Believe in the boogeyman if you want to, but not on the rest of us. We have our own boogeyman, and it isn't you.<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OTHER THAN THE JEWS[ONLY IF YOUR A HARD CORE JEW] NOBODY HAS A RIGHTWING REGILION BASED GOVERMENT THAT WORKS FOR THE PEOPLE EVER. SO WHY DO RUSH AND BUSH THINK IT IS A GOOD IDEA FOR THE HOMELAND?????????<P><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000070||ray b||10-20-2001||11:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B> Yeah, next you are going to tell us how we don't give any foreign aid to Arab countries. Or pump illions into their economies through the purchase of oil. And I think the Israeli's DO want to co-exist peacefully with their Arab neighbors. It's the radical Arabs who want to exterminate the Jews. In any order to maintain any semblance of order in their, Israel simply has to respond to Palestinian violence with the level of force that they do.<P>As far as the Mormons, you conveniently forgot to name any specific instances of the events you named. When were they at war with the USA? Why do you think they moved to Utah? Because intolerant people like you wouldn't leave them alone anywhere else, that's why. <BR>You are obviously so totally ignorant on these subjects that it is impossible to attempt to have any sort of rational debate with you. The amount of research, thought, and knowledge that you put into your posts appears to be about par with the effort you put into communicating in a coherent manner. Little to none.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>MORMANS RUN UTAH FOR THE MORMANS AND HAVE A HISTORY OF RUNING OUT ALL WHO ARE NOT IN THEIR CHURCH.AND HAVE SHUNDED BANNED AND EXCOMUNICATED ALL THEY SAY ARE NOT OF THE CHURCH. BUT TRY AND GET A STATE OR LOCAL GOV JOB IF YOUR NOT IN THE CHURCH AND SEE HOW THEY TREAT OTHERS.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000071||Formula88||10-20-2001||11:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>read list for christian con's [is there any other kind?]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Um, yes.  How about Pagan/Wiccan conservatives?  How about Jewish conservatives?  How about Muslim conservatives?  I've met examples of all three.  I'm a conservative Republican, and I don't like the Moral Majority.  It's my main complaint with the Republican platform.<P>Eds, <BR>I've not attacked your character.  I will disagree with you as I see fit, just as I'm sure you will disagree with me as you see fit.  Also, I've never needed a bandwagon to jump on when disagreeing with you.  If you feel people are ganging up on you, so be it.<P>As for the rest of this argument....  say what you will.  Freedom of speech is protected in America.  So spout on about your views for all I care.  I've made my points.<P>When a person does a stupid thing, you can tell them it is a stupid thing, but they have to decide whether or not to continue doing it.  <P>The definition of insanity is doing the same thing over and over expecting different results.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000072||maryjane||10-20-2001||12:19 PM||||I've clearly shown that power and greed, mixed in with predjudice are the root causes of strife and war. Hitler could have been raised as an athiest and would have done the same thing. You cannot realistically believe that Hitler believed in anything but himself and his master race propaganda. If no religion existed, he would have picked out something else to focus his hate upon; to blame all of Germany's problems on. Just as you are doing now. Who are "the people" Ray?<BR> Are you really saying that the Pope caused WWII? I doubt any Pope ever prayed for Hitler's victory. You're more intelligent than that! If we were in war against Japan on a religious basis, we would have turned the other cheek, after Pearl Harbor. It was for revenge and national survival, pride and honor. Buddist monks incinerate themselves as a way to bring focus to a cause, not because Buddha commands them to. <BR>I answered your challenge, you didn't want to see it, so you didn't. Who's in the Box, Ray?<BR>Have you not realized yet the futility of your belief that all religion is bad for everyone? If you think that for yourself, that's fine. It's your right, & I support that right. If religion would dis-appear totally, the strife and bloodshed would continue, it's in human nature. Jealousy, love, hate, greed. Human emotions and responses to those emotions are the cause of problems. Both on a personal scale and nationalist. People will always believe in something, that too is human nature. Even atheist believe in atheism so strongly that they blame all their problems on something else, no matter how ridicules it may be. It in itself becomes a religion of sorts. You are personal testimony to that. You are a self-confessed athiest, look how hard you argue for your cause. The hate is there, just as it was in Hitler, just focused on all religions instead of just the Jews. Focused on anyone not like yourself. That's predjudice and bigotry, Ray. An ugly side to any society. Sorry to say it, you're hateful sounding and bitter. <p>[This message has been edited by maryjane (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
